{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Dimensionality Reduction Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: PCA from scratch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class PCA:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, n_components):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.n_components = n_components"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.components = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.mean = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.eigenvalues = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.explained_variance_ratio_ = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def fit(self, X):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.mean = np.mean(X, axis=0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        X_centered = X - self.mean"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        cov_matrix = np.cov(X_centered, rowvar=False)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        eigenvalues, eigenvectors = np.linalg.eigh(cov_matrix)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        sorted_idx = np.argsort(eigenvalues)[::-1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        eigenvalues = eigenvalues[sorted_idx]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        eigenvectors = eigenvectors[:, sorted_idx]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.components = eigenvectors[:, :self.n_components].T"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.eigenvalues = eigenvalues[:self.n_components]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        total_var = np.sum(eigenvalues)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.explained_variance_ratio_ = self.eigenvalues / total_var"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def transform(self, X):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        X_centered = X - self.mean"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return X_centered @ self.components.T"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def fit_transform(self, X):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.fit(X)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.transform(X)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Test on synthetic data"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "np.random.seed(42)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "n_samples = 500"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "t = np.random.uniform(0, 2 * np.pi, n_samples)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "x1 = 3 * np.cos(t) + np.random.normal(0, 0.2, n_samples)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "x2 = 3 * np.sin(t) + np.random.normal(0, 0.2, n_samples)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "x3 = 0.5 * x1 + 0.3 * x2 + np.random.normal(0, 0.1, n_samples)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "X_synthetic = np.column_stack([x1, x2, x3])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "pca = PCA(n_components=2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "X_reduced = pca.fit_transform(X_synthetic)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Original shape: {X_synthetic.shape}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Reduced shape:  {X_reduced.shape}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Explained variance ratios: {pca.explained_variance_ratio_}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Total variance captured: {sum(pca.explained_variance_ratio_):.4f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: MNIST digits in 2D"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.datasets import fetch_openml"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "mnist = fetch_openml(\"mnist_784\", version=1, as_frame=False, parser=\"auto\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "X_mnist = mnist.data[:5000].astype(float)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "y_mnist = mnist.target[:5000].astype(int)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "pca_mnist = PCA(n_components=50)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "X_pca50 = pca_mnist.fit_transform(X_mnist)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"50 components capture {sum(pca_mnist.explained_variance_ratio_):.2%} of variance\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "pca_2d = PCA(n_components=2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "X_pca2d = pca_2d.fit_transform(X_mnist)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"2 components capture {sum(pca_2d.explained_variance_ratio_):.2%} of variance\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Compare with sklearn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.decomposition import PCA as SklearnPCA"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.manifold import TSNE"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "sklearn_pca = SklearnPCA(n_components=2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "X_sklearn_pca = sklearn_pca.fit_transform(X_mnist)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"\\nOur PCA explained variance:     {pca_2d.explained_variance_ratio_}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Sklearn PCA explained variance: {sklearn_pca.explained_variance_ratio_}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "diff = np.abs(np.abs(X_pca2d) - np.abs(X_sklearn_pca))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Max absolute difference: {diff.max():.10f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "tsne = TSNE(n_components=2, perplexity=30, random_state=42)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "X_tsne = tsne.fit_transform(X_mnist)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"\\nt-SNE output shape: {X_tsne.shape}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: UMAP comparison"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "try:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    from umap import UMAP"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    reducer = UMAP(n_components=2, n_neighbors=15, min_dist=0.1, random_state=42)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    X_umap = reducer.fit_transform(X_mnist)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"UMAP output shape: {X_umap.shape}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "except ImportError:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(\"Install umap-learn: pip install umap-learn\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Modify the PCA class to support `inverse_transform`. Reconstruct MNIST digits from 10, 50, and 200 components. Print the reconstruction error (mean squared difference from the original) for each.\n\n2. Run t-SNE on the same MNIST subset with perplexity values of 5, 30, and 100. Describe how the output changes. Why does perplexity affect cluster tightness?\n\n3. Take a dataset with 50 features where only 5 are informative (generate one with `sklearn.datasets.make_classification`). Apply PCA and check whether the explained variance curve correctly identifies that the data is effectively 5-dimensional."
      ]
    }
